---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base title="Rankings" section="rankings" description="Global Rank, Rank, and Level.">
  <div class="prose">
    <h1>Rankings</h1>
    <p class="lede">Global Rank, Rank, and Level. Nothing else.</p>
  </div>

  <section class="panel">
    <div class="panel__header">
      <span>Status</span>
      <span class="badge badge--warning">PROVISIONAL MODEL</span>
    </div>
    <div class="panel__body prose">
      <p>
        The ranking model in use is <code>provisional-v0</code>, and the API says so on every
        response. It is a difficulty-weighted sum over distinct solved Trials — deliberately simple,
        and deliberately not presented as a validated skill rating.
      </p>
      <p>What it does not do, and why not yet:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>No decay.</strong> That needs longitudinal data we do not have.</li>
        <li>
          <strong>No top-N weighting.</strong> Picking a coefficient today would mean inventing one and
          calling it science.
        </li>
        <li><strong>No population normalisation.</strong> That needs a population.</li>
        <li>
          <strong>No anti-grind weighting.</strong> That needs observed grinding to calibrate against.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        It is behind a trait and every stored score records which model produced it, so replacing
        the model is a recompute rather than a migration.
      </p>
      <h2>What a public profile shows</h2>
      <p>Exactly seven things, and the list is enforced by a test:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Username</li>
        <li>Clan, if any</li>
        <li>Global Rank</li>
        <li>Rank</li>
        <li>Level</li>
        <li>Trials solved</li>
        <li>Highest Trial milestone badge — one badge, upgraded in place</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Deliberately absent: country and regional rankings, public performance-history graphs,
        contribution heatmaps, course badges, stacked milestone badges, and tiered presentation.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <style>
    .lede {
      font-size: var(--step-1);
      color: var(--ink-muted);
      max-width: var(--measure);
    }
    section {
      margin-top: var(--space-5);
    }
  </style>
</Base>
